.TH std::inplace_vector::capacity 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::capacity \- std::inplace_vector::capacity

.SH Synopsis
static constexpr size_type capacity() noexcept;  (since C++26)

Returns the capacity of the internal (inplace) storage. Equivalent to: return N;.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

The maximum number of elements the container is able to hold.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Notes

Because each std::inplace_vector<T, N> is a fixed-capacity container, the value returned
by capacity equals N (which is also the value returned by max_size()).

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <inplace_vector>

int main()
{
    constexpr std::inplace_vector<int, 4> v1;
    static_assert(v1.capacity() == 4 && v1.max_size() == 4);

    constexpr std::inplace_vector<int, 0> v2;
    static_assert(v2.capacity() == 0 && v2.max_size() == 0);
}

